 true] [17592186284194 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534363 true] [17592186284194 1100 "The largest union of intervals on which the function $f(x)=\\frac{x+5}{{x}^{2}+2x-15}$ is continuous is\n\n$\\,(-\\infty ,$\n{{field-1}}$)⋃($\n{{field-2}},\n{{field-3}}$)⋃($\n{{field-4}}$,\\infty ).$" 13194139534363 true] [17592186284194 1113 #uuid "ad4ccf14-b5f3-5487-9d10-778581197e92" 13194139534363 true] [17592186284194 1145 "This is a rational function, so it is continuous at all points in its domain. To find its domain, we start by factoring the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{x+5}{{x}^{2}+2x-15} \\\\  & =\\frac{x+5}{{x}^{2}+5x-3x-15} \\\\  & =\\frac{x+5}{(x+5)(x-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x-3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $x\\ne -5.$\n\nThis function is continuous everywhere except at the excluded points $x=-5$ and $x=3.$\n\nTherefore, the domain consists of the union of the intervals $(-\\infty ,-5),$ $(-5,3),$ and $(3,\\infty ),$ namely\n\n$$\n(-\\infty ,-5)\\cup (-5,3)\\cup (3,\\infty )\n$$\n\nand the function is also continuous on this union of intervals." 13194139534363 true] [17592186284195 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284196 13194139534363 true] [17592186284195 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534363 true] [17592186284195 1041 "field-1" 13194139534363 true] [17592186284195 1104 #edb/ref 17592186284196 13194139534363 true] [17592186284195 1110 #uuid "4c06799e-0609-5d97-8a3b-929b3163db28" 13194139534363 true] [17592186284196 1034 "-5" 13194139534363 true] [17592186284196 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534363 true] [17592186284196 1111 #uuid "7b7e1433-afe9-5ad4-9757-6257dd75177f" 13194139534363 true] [17592186284197 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284198 13194139534363 true] [17592186284197 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534363 true] [17592186284197 1041 "field-2" 13194139534363 true] [17592186284197 1104 #edb/ref 17592186284198 13194139534363 true] [17592186284197 1110 #uuid "6acc179c-e9ef-5761-95ec-98d0f55d7221" 13194139534363 true] [175921862